# The root build context, reduced to what the root-context builds COPY.
#
# base and cloud build with `context: .` because they COPY _build/ and (cloud)
# _delta/components/. Without this file the WHOLE repository ships to the
# builder on every build — tests, fixtures, workflows, docs, .git — and every
# file in it is a cache input: a docs edit would not invalidate a layer (COPY
# is content-addressed), but the upload itself is waste, and anything
# accidentally COPYed later would ship silently. Allow-list, not deny-list:
# a NEW COPY source in base/ or cloud's Dockerfile must be added HERE or the
# build fails loudly at that COPY — which is the review moment working.
#
# The child images (flutter, embedded) build from their own
# directories; this file does not apply to their contexts. versions.env is
# deliberately absent: its values arrive as generated --build-arg, never COPY.
*
!_build
!_delta
